@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+---
+title: 'Self-employed coherence — referee checklist copy + employer/business label'
+type: 'bugfix'
+created: '2026-08-04'
+status: 'in-review'
+baseline_commit: 'b25b19c9d02d8106f2f2c279bbfbe708501812f1'
+review_loop_iteration: 0
+context: []
+---
+
+<frozen-after-approval reason="human-owned intent — do not modify unless human renegotiates">
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** For a self-employed applicant (sole trader) the checklist line "A written reference from your employer, if you're employed or self-employed" is incoherent — a reference from themselves? — and the required Work & Income field "Employer name" doesn't tell a sole trader to enter their trading name. User-ruled 2026-08-04 (screenshot-verified bug).
+
+**Approach:** Two label-only copy changes, applied uniformly: (1) replace the checklist line with the user-ruled sentence on every checklist surface; (2) relabel the `employer_name` field to "Employer / business name" and align its sibling display labels. Field names/ids (`employer_name`) are untouched — the AI scorer keys on the name, not the label.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Checklist copy is verbatim the user ruling: "A written reference from your employer — or from a client, accountant, or business contact if you're self-employed." One checklist everywhere (W1a doctrine): email HTML (`requirements_checklist_html`, shared by invite + auto-reply + both reminders) and the SSR form prep block.
+- Field label is verbatim "Employer / business name"; stays required when employment status = employed OR self-employed.
+- Email markup convention: em-dash as `&mdash;`; SSR form keeps literal `—` and `\u{2019}` per existing file style.
+- Sibling labels stay consistent: applicant error-summary label, co-applicant "Their employer", landlord-facing application detail + comparison fact row, audit-report PDF field-line.
+- Copy assertions updated to pin the new ruling (the old substring "written reference from your employer" still matches the new sentence, so strengthen assertions to pin the new clause).
+
+**Ask First:** none — copy is user-ruled verbatim.
+
+**Never:**
+- Do NOT rename the field name/id `employer_name`, JSON keys, DB columns, or scorer payload keys (label-only change).
+- Do NOT touch the refcheck referee-slot surfaces (`employer_ref_*` fields/labels: "Employer contact name", "Employer reference", "Employer ref" doc label, PDF "EMPLOYER REFERENCE") — separate track.
+- Do NOT touch AI-contract surfaces: `evidence_humanize` ("Stated employer", `employer_name:` → "Employer name:" excerpt derivation), `ai_client` payload keys. Note the "Employer name:" excerpt divergence in the PR instead.
+- Do NOT touch guarantor copy ("Employer or source of income" form label is already coherent; its PDF "Employer" line is a different field/person).
+- Do NOT touch `tenant-vetting-checklist.typ` (landlord-facing checklist, different copy/audience) — note as follow-up in PR.
+- No new dependencies, no JS FFI, no `let assert`.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Self-employed applicant reads checklist | Any checklist surface (invite, auto-reply, reminder 1/2, prep block) | New ruling sentence renders; old ", if you're employed or self-employed." phrasing gone | N/A |
+| Employed applicant | status = employed | Field labeled "Employer / business name", still required; checklist sentence unchanged for them (leads with employer) | N/A |
+| Validation error on employer_name | submit with empty employer_name, status employed/self-employed | Error summary shows "Employer / business name" (and "Other adult #N — Employer / business name" for co-applicant keys) | anchor/field ids unchanged |
+| Landlord reads application | detail page, comparison row, audit PDF | Value shown under "Employer / business name" | empty value → existing "Not specified"/dash fallbacks unchanged |
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
+
+## Code Map
+
+- `server/src/notification/email_client.gleam:245` — `requirements_checklist_html()`; one edit covers invite (:347), auto-reply (:422), reminder 1 (:480), reminder 2 (:545)
+- `server/src/application/form_view.gleam:145` — form-header prep block (`apply-prep-block`)
+- `server/src/application/form_sections/work_income.gleam:100` — the `employer_name` label
+- `server/src/application/error_summary.gleam:151` — `base_label("employer_name")`; also feeds "Other adult #N — …" co-applicant rows
+- `server/src/application/form_sections/situation.gleam:~345` — co-applicant `label: "Their employer"`
+- `client/src/pages/application_detail_data.gleam:82` — landlord detail `view_optional_field("Employer", …)`; :438 co-applicant card `"Employer: " <> n`
+- `client/src/pages/comparison/common_facts.gleam:67` — comparison `view_fact_row("Employer", …)`
+- `server/priv/templates/audit_report.typ:912` — `#field-line("Employer", …)` (git-tracked)
+- Tests: `server/test/application/form_view_test.gleam:362`, `server/test/notification/email_client_test.gleam:464,545` (+ auto-reply test block at :120)
+
+## Tasks & Acceptance
+
+**Execution:**
+- [x] `server/src/notification/email_client.gleam` — swap the checklist `<li>` for the ruled sentence (`&mdash;`) — covers invite, auto-reply, both reminders
+- [x] `server/src/application/form_view.gleam` — same sentence in the prep block (literal `—`, `\u{2019}`)
+- [x] `server/src/application/form_sections/work_income.gleam` — `label: "Employer / business name"`
+- [x] `server/src/application/error_summary.gleam` — `"employer_name" -> "Employer / business name"`
+- [x] `server/src/application/form_sections/situation.gleam` — co-applicant `label: "Their employer / business name"`
+- [x] `client/src/pages/application_detail_data.gleam` — `"Employer"` → `"Employer / business name"` (:82) and co-applicant card line (:438); do NOT touch `view_ref_block("Employer", …)` referee block (:280)
+- [x] `client/src/pages/comparison/common_facts.gleam` — fact row label; do NOT touch "Employer reference" row
+- [x] `server/priv/templates/audit_report.typ` — field-line label (:912) only; leave guarantor/co-applicant/referee lines
+- [ ] Tests — strengthen the three checklist assertions to pin the new clause; add an auto-reply checklist assertion; run format/test/build
+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given any checklist surface, when rendered, then it contains "or from a client, accountant, or business contact if you're self-employed" and no surface contains "employer, if you're employed or self-employed".
+- Given the Work & Income step, when status is employed OR self-employed, then the required field reads "Employer / business name" and validation/error-summary copy uses the same label.
+- Given a landlord view (detail, comparison, audit PDF), when employer_name is populated, then it displays under "Employer / business name".
+- `rg "written reference from your employer, if you"` is clean; `make format && make test && make build` green.
+
+## Design Notes
+
+Email vs SSR dash/quote style differ by file convention (email: `&mdash;` + literal `'`; SSR: literal `—` + `\u{2019}`) — match each file, keep the sentence otherwise identical. The scorer excerpt line "Employer name: …" (derived mechanically from the unchanged field key in `evidence_humanize`) and the AI source tag "Stated employer" intentionally stay as-is; flag both in the PR.
+
+## Verification
+
+**Commands:**
+- `make format && make test && make build` — green
+- `rg "employer, if you" server/ client/ shared/` — no matches
+- `rg "Employer name" server/src client/src` — no matches outside tests
+- `make test-integration` (own Docker DB container, non-default port) — green
+
+**Manual checks (if no CLI):**
+- Real-browser screenshot: `/apply/:code` Work & Income step with Self-employed selected (new label) against local Docker DB + seeded vacancy
+- Real-browser screenshot: rendered invite email HTML containing the new checklist line
